From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ns2kracy <ns2kracy@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:51:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] davsync: list R2 usage at the bucket root without moving
 existing objects

Reported and reproduced by Ns2Kracy. An R2 endpoint saved with a path
could read and write the setup and usage objects, but sent the usage
listing to an object path and failed with 404 NoSuchKey. Move that path
into the runtime object-key prefix, preserving the exact object URLs and
saved sync-state identity. Handle both addressing modes, reject a
conflicting path-style bucket, and keep non-R2 proxy paths unchanged.

Base: yetone/main 83545a5d8f84bad1076e85282ec916331f8c57f3.
Regression before the fix: all five cases of
TestS3R2EndpointPathKeepsObjectsAndListsBucket fail with HTTP 404
NoSuchKey; TestS3R2PathStyleEndpointNamesItsBucket accepts the conflicting
bucket. Both pass with the fix; the tests use signed local HTTP fixtures.

Verified under an isolated HOME with Go caches pinned:
- gofmt -l on both Go files: no output; git diff --check: clean.
- go test -tags nogui ./internal/davsync -count=1 -timeout=15m: ok.
- R2/proxy/address/shared-S3 tests with -race -count=5: ok.
- go test -tags nogui ./internal/cli -run TestS3Cmd -count=1: ok.
- Linux nogui and Windows go vet ./...: ok.
- Linux nogui and Windows builds: ok (outputs outside the checkout).

Not green/completed: the full nogui suite was stopped after about 19m.
The completed agent package failed TestAgyShell and TestGrokInstalled;
both fail unchanged at the exact base above too. The fish/POSIX fixture
mismatch is #5446, the WSL MZ fake binary issue is #3548. Other slow
packages had not finished; no full-suite pass is claimed. Native Linux
GUI vet/build are blocked by missing pkg-config. GUI browser tests and
native Windows execution were not run. This is submitted as a draft.

Real-use evidence was collected before rebasing: the existing R2 backup
HEAD returned 200 while the old listing returned 404; the corrected
listing and an existing usage download returned 200. An equivalent local
configuration correction preserved merge state and let the running
magpie finish usage sharing without error. No credentials or diagnostic
scripts are included.
